		zot:shortTitle "殖民地过去和现在的幽灵：贝尼托-佩雷斯-加尔多斯小说中的西班牙帝国主义贝尼托-佩雷斯-加尔多斯小说中的西班牙帝国主义" ;
		zot:dateModified "2024-12-12T20:59:10Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
		zot:tags <https://www.zotero.org/entities/tag/b16cd58d-8b07-5b62-b816-19eb5f526c45> , <https://www.zotero.org/entities/tag/3eb01dd9-c729-5464-af6a-cfdc05f061df> , <https://www.zotero.org/entities/tag/807b7762-2495-5a0c-8298-ff7931603bf9> , <https://www.zotero.org/entities/tag/2917eb8a-e885-541a-9a92-674c947922fe> , <https://www.zotero.org/entities/tag/132e1bb8-5a5b-5a57-ac7a-a0b23a484a73> , <https://www.zotero.org/entities/tag/cab770a6-73c8-5158-953f-9a351413b3f1> , <https://www.zotero.org/entities/tag/3d6cb796-3f18-5842-a0b5-888b392633e1> , <https://www.zotero.org/entities/tag/489a4e59-5115-5440-83a5-524268c303f4> , <https://www.zotero.org/entities/tag/26e342d2-3ad6-5d65-bbe3-d59074e50747> , <https://www.zotero.org/entities/tag/62fb2819-011e-512c-b5e5-98a12b7fe694> ;
		zot:callNumber "0" ;
		zot:key "T84PM72B" ;
		zot:inLibrary <https://www.zotero.org/groups/open-access_history_books> ;
		zot:libraryCatalog "0" ;
		owl:sameAs <https://library.oapen.org/handle/20.500.12657/46034?show=full> ;
		zot:abstractNote "Ghosts of Colonies Past and Present is the first comprehensive examination of how the literary production of Benito Pérez Galdós, widely considered Spain’s greatest nineteenth-century novelist, addresses the impact of imperial loss on the citizens of Spain. Well before the events that would lead inexorably toward 1898, Galdós’s texts question the nature of Spanish imperialism and the effect of colonial history on the lives of metropolitan citizens. Methodologically framed by trauma studies, affect studies and the concept of the imperial turn, a close reading of the texts reveals Galdós’s preoccupation with explaining not only how Spain lost its vast territories in the Americas in the early part of the century but also how Spanish citizens could manage the trauma of that loss through a reconfiguration of national identity. His novels reveal the deeply entwined nature of colonial relations and life in the metropolis. Moreover, by recognizing that the national response to the trauma of imperial loss extended across the nineteenth century, it becomes clear that Spain’s engagement with European cultural and literary movements was, contrary to the assumptions of European imperialism, neither slow nor imitative but rather illustrative of the nation’s unique position on the cusp of the historical shift to the postcolonial present.\n\n【摘要翻译】殖民地的过去和现在的幽灵》是对贝尼托-佩雷斯-加尔多斯（Benito Pérez Galdós）文学创作的首次全面研究，他被广泛认为是西班牙 19 世纪最伟大的小说家，他的文学创作探讨了帝国丧失对西班牙公民的影响。早在 1898 年事件发生之前，加尔多斯的作品就对西班牙帝国主义的本质以及殖民历史对大都市市民生活的影响提出了质疑。在创伤研究、情感研究和帝国转向概念的方法论框架下，对这些文本的细读揭示了加尔多斯不仅专注于解释西班牙如何在本世纪初失去其在美洲的大片领土，而且专注于解释西班牙公民如何通过重新配置国家身份来处理这种损失带来的创伤。他的小说揭示了殖民关系与大都市生活的深刻纠葛。此外，通过认识到西班牙对帝国丧失所造成的创伤的反应跨越了整个 19 世纪，我们可以清楚地看到，与欧洲帝国主义的假设相反，西班牙对欧洲文化和文学运动的参与既不是缓慢的，也不是模仿性的，而是说明了西班牙在历史转向后殖民时代的风口浪尖上所处的独特地位。" ;
