		zot:abstractNote "Empire and Environment argues that histories of imperialism, colonialism, militarism, and global capitalism are integral to understanding environmental violence in the transpacific region. The collection draws its rationale from the imbrication of imperialism and global environmental crisis, but its inspiration from the ecological work of activists, artists, and intellectuals across the transpacific region. Taking a postcolonial, ecocritical approach to confronting ecological ruin in an age of ecological crises and environmental catastrophes on a global scale, the collection demonstrates how Asian North American, Asian diasporic, and Indigenous Pacific Island cultural expressions critique a de-historicized sense of place, attachment, and belonging. In addition to its thirteen chapters from scholars who span the Pacific, each part of this volume begins with a poem by Craig Santos Perez. The volume also features a foreword by Macarena Gómez-Barris and an afterword by Priscilla Wald.\n\n【摘要翻译】帝国与环境》认为，帝国主义、殖民主义、军国主义和全球资本主义的历史对于理解泛太平洋地区的环境暴力不可或缺。这本文集的理论基础来自帝国主义与全球环境危机的交织，而灵感则来自跨太平洋地区活动家、艺术家和知识分子的生态工作。在全球生态危机和环境灾难频发的时代，本文集采用后殖民主义和生态批判的方法来面对生态破坏，展示了北美亚裔、亚裔散居者和太平洋岛屿土著的文化表现形式如何批判去历史化的地方感、依恋感和归属感。除了来自太平洋地区学者的 13 个章节外，本文集的每个部分都以克雷格-桑托斯-佩雷斯的一首诗作为开头。本卷还收录了 Macarena Gómez-Barris 的前言和 Priscilla Wald 的后记。" ;
